      "body": "## Overview\n\nFix the async warmup failure regression test for Triton's new `cleanup_fn` argument while retaining compatibility with Triton 3.8. AI assistance (Codex) was used; this draft is for human review.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The test reaches its intended compile-failure and context-restoration assertions instead of failing at `AsyncCompileMode.submit()` argument binding.\n- Signature inspection supplies the no-op cleanup callback only when supported. Production code and the existing assertions are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nExecuted the upstream test file in a CUDA sandbox using Python 3.14.7 and Triton `3.9.0.dev20261027+cuda.13.4.sm120.znver4.ga5f620fa`. The installed vLLM runtime is our fork; its original warmup modules were restored during this validation so the separate compiler fixes were not involved.\n\n```sh\nPYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=2 \\\n  /opt/trim-wheels-20261030/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  --noconftest --import-mode=importlib -q --tb=short \\\n  /opt/trim-wheels-20261030/test_upstream_async_cleanup.py\n```\n\nThe file above is a copy of this PR's test file. Before the fix, the affected case failed with `TypeError: AsyncCompileMode.submit() missing 1 required positional argument: 'cleanup_fn'`. After the fix, the complete file reports **15 passed**.\n\nAlso executed the exact patched submission block with the official Triton v3.8.0 and current main `_async_compile.py` implementations. Both propagated the intended `RuntimeError(\"warmup failed\")` and cleared `active_mode`. This checks both API shapes, rather than claiming a full Triton 3.8 environment run.\n\n`pre-commit run --files tests/model_executor/test_jit_warmup_triton_launcher.py`, Ruff check/format, and `git diff --check` pass. Model evaluation is not applicable to this test-only change.\n\n## Details\n\n[triton-lang/triton#11552](https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/pull/11552) added the required cleanup callback. Triton v3.8.0 still has the three-argument form, so unconditionally adding a fourth argument would break that version. The test inspects the supported signature and preserves the same failure injection for both forms.\n\nChecked open upstream PRs for `cleanup_fn warmup` and `AsyncCompileMode submit`; no duplicate was found. No public serving behavior, documentation, or kernel math changes.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimal test compatibility fix; no production changes.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Failure reproduced, full test file passes, both API shapes exercised.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Existing test and assertions retained; lint passes.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes root cause, compatibility scope, and precise validation limits.\n</details>\n",
